\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.7}{\ignorespaces Continuous-integration pipeline. A single push triggers five parallel GitHub Actions workflows: \texttt  {api.yml} (backend tests against real PostgreSQL and Redis service containers), \texttt  {lint.yml} (Ruff + mypy on the Python tree), \texttt  {web.yml} (TypeScript compile, ESLint, and the \texttt  {check:api-types} gate), \texttt  {mobile.yml} (Expo prebuild + Jest), and \texttt  {models.yml} (model-artefact hash verification). The \texttt  {api.yml} job runs against real service containers rather than mocks to ensure that Alembic migrations, which mocked tests cannot exercise, are validated on every push.}}{70}{figure.4.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ch4:ci}{{4.7}{70}{Continuous-integration pipeline. A single push triggers five parallel GitHub Actions workflows: \texttt {api.yml} (backend tests against real PostgreSQL and Redis service containers), \texttt {lint.yml} (Ruff + mypy on the Python tree), \texttt {web.yml} (TypeScript compile, ESLint, and the \texttt {check:api-types} gate), \texttt {mobile.yml} (Expo prebuild + Jest), and \texttt {models.yml} (model-artefact hash verification). The \texttt {api.yml} job runs against real service containers rather than mocks to ensure that Alembic migrations, which mocked tests cannot exercise, are validated on every push}{figure.4.7}{}}
