\newlabel{fig:ch4:wazuhrules}{{4.19}{79}{Custom Wazuh rule hierarchy. Parent rules 80789, 80784 and 80785 are forced to \texttt {level=0} so they do not flood the alert stream; the child rules 100050, 100051, 100100+ and 100200+ inherit through \texttt {$\langle $if\_sid$\rangle $} and only fire when the parent matches a specific attacker pattern}{figure.4.19}{}}
