\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.23}{\ignorespaces The gating logic that wraps every DQN action. An intervention (\texttt  {ESCALATE}, \texttt  {ISOLATE\_HOST}, \texttt  {BLOCK\_USER\_IP}) is only authorised when all four deterministic checks (AE score, $\beta $-VAE probability, Transformer confidence and GNN node risk) exceed their thresholds. Any single failure down-grades the action to \texttt  {LOW\_ALERT}.}}{84}{figure.4.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ch4:dqngating}{{4.23}{84}{The gating logic that wraps every DQN action. An intervention (\texttt {ESCALATE}, \texttt {ISOLATE\_HOST}, \texttt {BLOCK\_USER\_IP}) is only authorised when all four deterministic checks (AE score, $\beta $-VAE probability, Transformer confidence and GNN node risk) exceed their thresholds. Any single failure down-grades the action to \texttt {LOW\_ALERT}}{figure.4.23}{}}
